<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?> <rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"> <channel> <title>Top of Mind</title><description>Landon&#39;s personal life and coding blog</description><link>https://topofmind.dev/</link><atom:link href="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /> <managingEditor>Landon Clipp</managingEditor><docs>https://github.com/LandonTClipp/LandonTClipp.github.io</docs><language>en</language> <pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 21:29:49 -0000</pubDate> <lastBuildDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 21:29:49 -0000</lastBuildDate> <ttl>1440</ttl> <generator>MkDocs RSS plugin - v1.17.4</generator> <image> <url>None</url> <title>Top of Mind</title> <link>https://topofmind.dev/</link> </image> <item> <title>Pilgrimage</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Life</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;It&#39;s not even the normal time of year for reflection on what has happened in the last twelve months, but these last four months have compressed within them what feels like a lifetime, so reflection seems unavoidable. I began this year with one measure of hope and another measure of deep dissatisfaction. I still had it in my head last January that life would go my way, that the plan I had devised for myself, for my small family of two, would unfold more or less accordingly.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Oh, how life likes to utterly fuck things up.&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/09/01/pilgrimage/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/09/01/pilgrimage/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-09-01-pilgrimage.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>The Dawn of Break</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description></description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/26/the-dawn-of-break/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/26/the-dawn-of-break/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-08-26-the-dawn-of-break.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>The Woman in the Corner</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Taken from a perspective that is not my own.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/25/the-woman-in-the-corner/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/25/the-woman-in-the-corner/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-08-25-the-woman-in-the-corner.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>The Power of Now</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Life</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;&#34; src=&#34;https://assets.topofmind.dev/posts/2026-08-22-the-power-of-now/IMG_1145.jpeg&#34;&gt;{ style=&#34;width: 100%; height: 300px; object-fit: cover; object-position: 0 30%&#34; }&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Five years ago, I first came to the mountains of the western United States. The trip was one of obligation, although an obligation I accepted willingly: the wedding of my girlfriend&#39;s (soon to be wife&#39;s) cousin and his bride. It sometimes happens that ordinary moments acquire extraordinary meaning only in retrospect. Looking back, I understand that this trip was never merely a story about attending a wedding or supporting my wife’s family.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;It was the story of finding my home. And, in a way I would not understand until years later, it was the story of finding God.&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/22/the-power-of-now/</link> <pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/22/the-power-of-now/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-08-22-the-power-of-now.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Upheaval</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Life</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;Far be it from me to be religious in the traditional sense. Those who know me know my embattled history with religion in my younger years. Still, I can&#39;t help but draw upon the ancient stories of the past to seek wisdom and parallels with the trials I face in life.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;In the book of Exodus, the Israelites did not leave Egypt because they knew what came next. They left because they could no longer remain where they were. Generations of Israelites had lived in Egypt until a new Pharaoh came to see their growing population as a threat. He subjected them to forced labor, ordered increasingly brutal measures against them, and eventually commanded that their newborn sons be killed. Their suffering became so great that the story says their cries rose to God, who called Moses to lead them out of Egypt.&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/11/upheaval/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/08/11/upheaval/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-08-11-upheaval.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>The Empty Side</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description></description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/27/the-empty-side/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/27/the-empty-side/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-07-27-lay-back-down.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Beyond the Burn</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description></description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/04/beyond-the-burn/</link> <pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/04/beyond-the-burn/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-07-04-renewal.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Interstitial</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;&#34; src=&#34;https://assets.topofmind.dev/posts/2026-07-03-interstitial/f840c610-a557-44af-8866-363a814cda71.png&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/03/interstitial/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/03/interstitial/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-07-03-interstitial.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>The Fire</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description></description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/03/the-fire/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/07/03/the-fire/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-07-03-the-fire.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>I Don&#39;t Know How I Got Here</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Career</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;&#34; src=&#34;https://assets.topofmind.dev/posts/2026-06-09-i-dont-know-how-i-got-here/IMG_0641.jpeg&#34;&gt;{ loading=lazy style=&#34;object-fit: cover;&#34;}&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;One of my favorite life philosophies is something everyone has heard: it&#39;s better to ask for forgiveness than permission. I&#39;m currently sitting outside by an alpine river in the San Juan mountains called Mineral Creek, which is situated downstream of two high alpine lakes called Ice Lake and Island Lake. I was forced to this spot not by choice, but because I had overstayed my welcome at my last campsite at the top of this place called Molas Pass. I knew I was over the 14 day limit, but I wasn&#39;t sure how strictly it was enforced. Apparently, very strictly. A Bureau of Land Management Police Officer knocked on my trailer door around noon, seemingly disappointed in me.&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/06/09/i-dont-know-how-i-got-here/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/06/09/i-dont-know-how-i-got-here/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-06-09-i-dont-know-how-i-got-here.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Gives But A Step Into The Night</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description>&lt;div class=&#34;poem&#34; markdown&gt; ![](https://assets.topofmind.dev/posts/2026-06-05-gives-but-a-step-into-the-night/gives-but-a-step-into-the-night.png)</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/06/05/gives-but-a-step-into-the-night/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 05 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/06/05/gives-but-a-step-into-the-night/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-06-05-gives-but-a-step-into-the-night.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Candlelight</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Poems</category> <description>&lt;div class=&#34;poem&#34; markdown&gt; ![](https://assets.topofmind.dev/posts/2026-06-02-candlelight/candlelight.png)</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/06/02/candlelight/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 02 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/06/02/candlelight/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-06-02-candlelight.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>GPU Virtualization Part 2: IOMMUs and Hardware Isolation</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>GPU Virtualization</category> <category>System Design</category> <description>A focused look into how IOMMUs work and why it&#39;s critical for isolating PCIe fabrics.</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/05/08/gpu-virtualization-part-2-iommus-and-hardware-isolation/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 08 May 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/05/08/gpu-virtualization-part-2-iommus-and-hardware-isolation/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-05-08-iommu-and-hardware-isolation.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>GPU Virtualization Part 1: An Introduction to PCIe and MMIO</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>GPU Virtualization</category> <category>System Design</category> <description>Understanding foundational technologies for GPU virtualization and sandboxing.</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/02/15/gpu-virtualization-part-1-an-introduction-to-pcie-and-mmio/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Feb 2026 12:00:00 -0600</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/02/15/gpu-virtualization-part-1-an-introduction-to-pcie-and-mmio/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-02-15-pcie-mmio.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Goodbye Lambda, Hello CoreWeave</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Career</category> <description>A proper farewell to a group I hope to one day work with again.</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/01/21/goodbye-lambda-hello-coreweave/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Jan 2026 12:00:00 -0600</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/01/21/goodbye-lambda-hello-coreweave/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-01-21-goodbye-lambda.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>My AI Infra Thesis of 2026</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>System Design</category> <description>My years-long bet of AI infrastructure and how it will shape the major cloud providers.</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/01/01/my-ai-infra-thesis-of-2026/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 01 Jan 2026 12:00:00 -0600</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2026/01/01/my-ai-infra-thesis-of-2026/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026-01-01-ai-infra-thesis.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Out With Google Analytics, In With Cloudflare</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Misc</category> <category>System Design</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;Readers of my blog have unknowingly been contributing to something I shamefully admit: I&#39;ve been tracking you. I know when you view my blog site, where you&#39;re from, what you&#39;re looking at, when you click on elements, and for how long you stay on my pages. This is made quite simple, actually. However, I realized my site tracking is no longer totally effective, and I found another easy way around it. This is how.&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/12/28/out-with-google-analytics-in-with-cloudflare/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 28 Dec 2025 12:00:00 -0600</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/12/28/out-with-google-analytics-in-with-cloudflare/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2025-12-28-out-with-analytics.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Colorado San Juan Mountains</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>RV</category> <description>The last trip of 2025 to Colorado.</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/12/09/colorado-san-juan-mountains/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 09 Dec 2025 12:00:00 -0600</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/12/09/colorado-san-juan-mountains/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2025-12-09-san-juan-mountains.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>Boot-time Performance of Kata Containers With NVIDIA GPUs</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Cloud</category> <category>System Design</category> <description>&lt;p&gt;If you recall in my &lt;a href=&#34;2025-10-21-gpu-containers-as-a-service.md&#34;&gt;previous post&lt;/a&gt;, we looked into how to utilize Kata VMs to create a multi-tenant, GPU-based Kubernetes cluster. We briefly mentioned various performance problems related to the VM boot process. This post will dive deeper into this issue and shed some insight into where time is being spent during the VM boot.&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/11/19/boot-time-performance-of-kata-containers-with-nvidia-gpus/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 19 Nov 2025 12:00:00 -0600</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/11/19/boot-time-performance-of-kata-containers-with-nvidia-gpus/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2025-11-19-gpu-passthrough-boot.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> <item> <title>GPU-based Containers as a Service</title> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <author>Landon Clipp</author> <category>Cloud</category> <category>System Design</category> <description>Designing a multi-tenant, GPU-based Kubernetes Cluster</description> <link>https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/10/21/gpu-based-containers-as-a-service/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 21 Oct 2025 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate> <source url="https://topofmind.dev/feed_rss_updated.xml">Top of Mind</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://topofmind.dev/blog/2025/10/21/gpu-based-containers-as-a-service/</guid> <enclosure url="https://topofmind.dev/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2025-10-21-gpu-containers-as-a-service.png" type="image/png" length="None" /> </item> </channel> </rss>